#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / GRUB2 Specification
PACKAGE: grub2
LANGUAGE: C, configuration, platform-specific tooling
STATUS: W2
ROLE: Bootloader and boot configuration generation

## PROGRAM
GRUB2 establishes the bootloader environment and hands execution to the selected kernel/initramfs configuration.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream GRUB2 / Ubuntu package
BOUNDARY: firmware/boot -> GRUB configuration -> kernel/initramfs -> operating system
WHITE_EDITION: deterministic configuration and recovery overlay
GUI: safe inspection/configuration only; privileged boot writes require explicit authorization and recovery safeguards

## SPEC
- deterministic boot artifacts
- documented recovery path
- explicit kernel/initramfs/encryption coordination
- preserve supported Ubuntu boot behavior

## QUALITY
TEST: artifact generation, configuration validation, kernel handoff, encrypted-root handoff, recovery boot, upgrade/regeneration
ECONOMY: artifact size, generation time, boot-path complexity

## SOURCE POLICY
Prefer configuration generation and packaging. Native C/platform changes require concrete boot/security need and platform evidence.
